Button labels must remain on one line.

Never place a heading and subtitle inside a button.

Never create tall buttons containing multiple lines of text.

Use icons where appropriate, but ensure the button label remains readable.

For icon-only buttons, provide tooltips and accessible labels.

Avoid excessive rounded pill buttons. Use a consistent, professional radius.

## 2.3 Typography

Use a modern, highly readable font such as Inter.

Establish consistent typography for:

- Page titles.
- Section headings.
- Table headers.
- Body text.
- Secondary descriptions.
- Form labels.
- Financial figures.
- Status labels.

