## 7.4 Financial ledger

Treat this as one of the highest-priority modules.

Implement:

- Double-entry accounting.
- Integer-based monetary calculations.
- Debit/credit conservation.
- Append-only financial records.
- Hash chaining.
- Reversal journals.
- Dual authorization where required.
- Transactional integrity.
- Idempotent financial operations.
- Reconciliation.

Use BigInt or an equivalent safe integer representation for monetary calculations.

Never use floating-point arithmetic for money.

Implement and test concurrency-safe hash chaining with a dedicated tenant-level chain-head mechanism.

Ensure a failed financial transaction cannot leave partially committed financial records.

Do not silently modify completed journals.

## 7.5 Auction engine

Implement the auction lifecycle properly.

Support the required auction modes through clearly defined state machines.

Implement:

- Auction creation.
- Lot assignment.
- Auction scheduling.
- Bid validation.
- Bid ordering.
- Buyer credit verification.
- Credit reservations.
- Winning bid identification.
- Auction closure.
- Sale confirmation.
- Cancellation.
- Audit history.

For real-time bidding, use a clearly defined authoritative ordering mechanism.

Do not use client timestamps as the authority for bid ordering.

Handle concurrent bids, duplicate submissions, reconnects and server failures.

Implement partial lot allocations if supported by the business workflow.

Do not enforce one sale per lot if partial sales are permitted.

## 7.6 Offline synchronization

Implement offline functionality for actual dockside workflows.

Use local encrypted storage where appropriate.

Implement:

- Local operation queues.
- UUIDv7 identifiers.
- Idempotency keys.
- Sync status.
- Retry logic.
- Conflict detection.
- Conflict resolution.
- Supervisor review.
- Synchronization audit logs.

Do not allow offline devices to independently finalize conflicting financial settlements or authoritative remote auctions.

Define exactly which operations are allowed offline.

## 7.7 Payment integrations

Implement a payment-provider abstraction.

Do not assume Razorpay Route, Cashfree or Stripe Connect will approve every proposed settlement arrangement.

Build:

- Payment intent tracking.
- Payment status.
- Payment references.
- Provider webhook handling.
- Signature verification.
- Idempotent webhook processing.
- Reconciliation.
- Refund/reversal workflows where supported.
- Settlement tracking.

Support manual payment and bank/UPI reconciliation as a fully functional alternative.

Do not fabricate successful provider transactions.

Keep statutory allocations and commercial platform fees configurable and versioned.

Do not activate disputed or legally unverified revenue deductions.

